## Key Concepts

- Machine learning models need training data.
- Bad training data can make the model less accurate.
- The model learns patterns from examples.
- More examples can help the model improve.
- The shape classifier was trained on stars, circles, and triangles.
- The model could then guess a new shape.
- The training was done locally on the computer.
- ML5.js was used to make the machine learning code easier.

## What is a Shape Classifier?

A shape classifier is a small machine learning model that tries to identify what someone draws.

In class, we drew stars, circles, and triangles to create the training data. After training, we could draw another shape and the model would guess what it was, it gave it a probability score. 

The model was not really looking at an image. It kept track of the points that were drawn and used those points as the data.

